ns row and use must_change_paths as a checklist; fixing only the first row is invalid.  Returning the same rejected content is not a correction. Valid parseable outputs are repaired by incremental operations under typed validator permissions, never by repeating the full object. If no output_patch_contract is supplied, return the normal full role object (no parseable correction base exists). When output_patch_contract is supplied, return exactly {\"base_hash\":\"the issued base_hash\",\"operations\":[...]}. Return changes only, never the full object or unchanged siblings. Each operation has op and path; replace/add/append also have value. Use only issued permissions. All indices address the same base snapshot, not a progressively shortened list. replace changes one value, remove deletes one authorized member, add creates a missing dictionary key, and append adds one new list member. Do not replace a whole existing list. Omitted fields are preserved by the runtime. The merged full object must still satisfy every original contract and validation obligation.",
